            "pages": {
              "end": 3,
              "start": 3
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Petitioners argue that the Age Discrimination in Employment Act (ADEA) bars employment practices that cause a significant disparate impact on older workers when those practices lack a reasonable business justification."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Mr. Nager",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "4dee917af5717fd9cb9ccf118ae6d99303df3413f3189ae31bae73e5ec1703fd",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-4dee917af571-0001-0003"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 25,
              "start": 25
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Mr. Nager, respondents contend that statistical correlations with age alone do not establish a prima facie case of age discrimination."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Fifth Circuit",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "4dee917af5717fd9cb9ccf118ae6d99303df3413f3189ae31bae73e5ec1703fd",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-4dee917af571-0003-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 53,
              "start": 53
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Fifth Circuit, respondents also argue that the \u201creasonable factors other than age\u201d (RFOA) provision is part of the ADEA, not Title\u202fVII."
      }
    ],
    "heading": "Overview",
    "status": "complete",
    "summary": null,
    "summary_citations": []
  },
  "party_positions": [
    {
      "claims": [
        {
          "attribution": "Petitioners",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "4dee917af5717fd9cb9ccf118ae6d99303df3413f3189ae31bae73e5ec1703fd",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-4dee917af571-0000-0002"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 3,
                "start": 3
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Petitioners, the ADEA prohibits employment practices that have a significant disparate impact on older workers if those practices lack a reasonable business justification."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Mr. Goldstein",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "4dee917af5717fd9cb9ccf118ae6d99303df3413f3189ae31bae73e5ec1703fd",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-4dee917af571-0001-0002"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 20,
                "start": 20
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Mr. Goldstein, petitioners cite EEOC cases, such as the Francis\u202fW.\u202fParker case, as examples of rules that prohibit hiring individuals who previously earned a higher salary, illustrating the need for a business justification."
        }
      ],
      "heading": "Petitioners",
      "status": "complete",
      "summary": null,
      "summary_citations": []
    },
    {
      "claims": [
        {
          "attribution": "Mr. Nager",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "4dee917af5717fd9cb9ccf118ae6d99303df3413f3189ae31bae73e5ec1703fd",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-4dee917af571-0001-0003"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 25,
                "start": 25
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Mr. Nager, statistical correlations with age alone do not create a prima facie case of age discrimination."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Fifth Circuit",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "4dee917af5717fd9cb9ccf118ae6d99303df3413f3189ae31bae73e5ec1703fd",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-4dee917af571-0003-0000"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 53,
                "start": 53
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Fifth Circuit, the \u201creasonable factors other than age\u201d provision is found in the ADEA, not in Title\u202fVII."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Mr. Goldstein",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "4dee917af5717fd9cb9ccf118ae6d99303df3413f3189ae31bae73e5ec1703fd",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-4dee917af571-0003-0002"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 54,
                "start": 54
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Mr. Goldstein, because the statute refers to something otherwise unlawful, it cannot be interpreted like the Price\u202fWaterhouse mixed\u2011motive doctrine."
        }
      ],
